{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Follow-up to the closed P1 bug rubied-nonvagrant-whimbrel (dd30-f10d-69f3-4c36), whose code fix is merged (13e2ea6decc9c62484f80034e28cb96c20448ea2): the three unescaped ${...} sites in infra/terraform/user_data.sh comments were reworded, `terraform plan` now exits 0, and a regression guard (scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py) is wired into `make lint`. That satisfied the bug's DoD (AC1: `terraform plan` completes).\n\nDEFERRED DEPLOYMENT DECISION (out of the original bug's envelope):\nThe pending `terraform plan` recorded on rubied reports `Plan: 6 to add, 1 to change, 0 to destroy`:\n- 2 new CloudWatch alarms: `mcp_mem_abort` and `mcp_retire_cap`\n- in-place update of `aws_instance.gerrit` user_data\n- 4 new `rebar_secrets` SSM params for MCP client PATs\nThe three `import` blocks in the plan are already adopted as no-op.\n\nRunning `terraform apply` against prod touches infrastructure beyond the dd30 bug's blast radius and is an OPERATOR DECISION requiring explicit human approval. This ticket tracks that go/no-go apply decision; it must NOT be executed autonomously by an agent.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] An operator explicitly reviews the recorded plan (6 add / 1 change / 0 destroy) and approves or rejects the `terraform apply`.\n- [ ] If approved, the apply is performed by/with a human operator and the resulting state is recorded back on this ticket.\n\n## Verification\n- `terraform plan` in `infra/terraform` must match the approved scope: 6 adds, 1 in-place `aws_instance.gerrit` user_data change, and 0 destroys.\n- Pause the discovered autodeploy systemd timer/unit for the apply window, record the exact unit name in a ticket comment, then re-enable it.\n- After apply, verify Gerrit, review-bot, opcert, and MCP health and confirm the autodeploy timer completes one clean cycle.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788763686897945001,"uuid":"234c6315-ef28-43ae-9d10-7359803097e3"}